# Dependencies, caches and build output — at any depth.
**/node_modules/
**/.cache/
**/.vite/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/coverage/

# Environment and secrets.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Logs and OS noise.
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local editor / agent state. The shared settings.json IS tracked; only the
# machine-local override is not.
**/.claude/settings.local.json

# Playwright runtime and session directories. These are driver state, written on
# every browser run — never project source.
**/.playwright/
**/.playwright-cli/
**/.playwright-mcp/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# _buro test 1 — regenerated artefacts, not sources.
#
# Scoped to this project on purpose. `_buro test 2` keeps its own
# assets/source/ because the pipeline reads from it and the generated frames in
# it are NOT reproducible: the model is non-deterministic, so a re-run produces a
# different image even from the recorded prompt.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/_buro test 1/assets/source/
/_buro test 1/assets/models/*.raw.glb
/_buro test 1/public/decoders/

# A stray verification capture at the project root. previews/ is the place for
# deliberate ones; a screenshot dropped beside index.html is scratch.
/_buro test 2/act00.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Screencast frames. The recorder writes one JPEG per delivered frame and the
# encoder turns them into the mp4 that IS the deliverable — 8,173 of them and
# 688 MB went into a commit once, which is what a push that never finishes
# looks like. The mp4s under exploration/review-video/ stay tracked.
**/frames-*/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# _buro test 2 — DCC source for the tree silhouettes. 409 MB of .blend, .fbx,
# a .rar of textures and raw maps, two of which are over GitHub's 100 MB hard
# limit and got a push rejected outright. Nothing at runtime reads any of it:
# the site loads models/tree-N.glb, which are the exports. The README and the
# conversion scripts stay tracked, because HOW the exports were made is the
# part worth keeping.
/_buro test 2/3D/*
!/_buro test 2/3D/README.md
!/_buro test 2/3D/convert-*.py
